  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "This medium is for co-culture of strain JT with Methanospirillum hungatei strain NBRC 100397."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "For vial cultures, dissolve all ingredients except for Na-terephthalate, Na2S·9H2O and cysteine-HCl (up to 900ml), flush N2/CO2 (80/20), and autoclave.  Add 0.5 ml of each of filter-sterilized Na2S·9H2O solution (0.6g Na2S·9H2O/50 ml) and cysteine-HCl solution (0.6g cysteine-HCl/ 50ml) per each vial separately.  Add 0.2 ml of neutralized and filter-sterilized 0.2 M Na-terephthalate solution. Yeast extract is also added at final concentration about 0.02%.  Inoculum size 10-20%.  Growth was observed after 3-4 weeks of incubation."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "First dissolve NTA in 200 ml of water and adjust the pH to 6.5 with KOH."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}